      "title": "\u2018We don\u2019t need people like that on earth\u2019: Parisians on the riots that shook France",
      "description": "Subhead:One week after a student protest turned into looting and fires across France, I went to Place de la R\u00e9publique to ask Parisians who did it and what comes next.# YouTube-embed:avbeRujyO5s I was in Paris on October 24, near Place de la R\u00e9publique. A week earlier, on Saturday, October 17, a student protest there turned into a riot, with shops looted and burned in Paris and in other cities across France. A woman who lives in the neighbourhood told me she supported the march but not the looters. \u201cI was mostly sad for the shopkeepers,\u201d she said. A man said he understood the anger but not the destruction. \u201cThey steal sneakers, they steal alcohol, they smash the PMU bar next door. You have to shout, but not like that.\u201d An elderly man who served in a commando unit in the 1950s said that back then, they opened fire. \u201cThere were deaths, fine, but they didn\u2019t do it again.\u201d When I asked who did the looting, people split. \u201cAngry people, poor people,\u201d one resident said. \u201cNobody steals for pleasure.\u201d An older man disagreed. \u201cThey\u2019re people from elsewhere, madame. People who are here to wreck things.\u201d",
